---
app: outline
title: An essay on small software
---
- Small software
  - The claim
    - A program can be finished
    - Finished programs are rare because nobody is paid to stop
  - Three examples
    - The pocket calculator
    - The text editor that has not changed since 1991
    - A spreadsheet of one table
  - The objection
    - Needs change, so programs must
    - Answer: needs change less than vendors say
  - What it would take
    - A format a person can read
    - No account to keep alive
    - A link that is the whole thing
